*
# Deny by default, then re-include only what the API image needs. This covers
# the uv workspace (every member's pyproject is needed to honour uv.lock), the
# migrations, and the repo-relative data files the API reads at runtime.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!alembic.ini
!migrations/
!packages/
!services/
!observability/
!infra/
!docs/legal/
# INT-465: the life-threat set the synthetic host serves under the test-key
# signature (INTAKE_API_TRIAGE_RULES). Only this one file from files/: the
# signature binds its exact bytes, and the rest of files/ is the spec.
!files/protocols/base.life_threat.yaml
# INT-187: the SLO files, which the release gate deploy.sh runs reads to
# evaluate the error budget (and the reliability console reads for its tiles).
!docs/slo/
# Never sent, wherever they sit. The host's root-only env file lives outside
# the tree (/etc/intake-staging), and these rules catch a stray copy anyway.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.cache
**/dist
packages/embed-sdk
